# Sprint Chunk Review/Test/Handoff Loop

For each sprint chunk/sub-task, use the same minimum gate before moving to the next chunk.

1. Lock target scope:
   - confirm active task ID, acceptance criteria, in-scope files, and out-of-scope boundaries
2. Review implementation scope:
   - ensure the diff stays inside the active task and does not introduce unrelated changes
   - keep package placement/layering aligned with project conventions
3. Run chunk-level validation:
   - run tests for touched behavior first
   - if contracts or persistence seams changed, run the nearest broader backend slice
4. Compare against sprint outcomes:
   - map results to task acceptance criteria and sprint Definition of Done invariants
5. Prepare handoff notes:
   - list files changed, tests run, intentionally deferred items, and open risks/questions
   - update the active sprint doc's execution status block so current, next, blocked, and completed chunks remain visible without re-reading the whole plan
6. Commit the chunk:
   - one commit per task; stage only this task's changes; message format `<type>(<scope>): E<epic> T<task> <subject>`; do not push unless the user asks. In Cursor use `.cursor/skills/commit-message/SKILL.md`; for Codex or when the skill is unavailable use `docs/sprint-execution-contract.md`
7. Apply go/no-go gate:
   - proceed to next chunk only when scope is clean, tests pass, sprint/spec docs are synced, and the chunk commit is created
